From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 55/55] Park destroyed buffer views until their buffer or device is destroyed

DXVK creates and destroys uniform texel buffer views on shared dynamic buffer
chunks every frame. Destroying a buffer view on the host removes its Metal
texture view from the device residency set and releases it while earlier queue
submissions referencing that view are still executing on the GPU, causing Metal
command buffer execution to fail with Invalid Resource (code 9), while each
re-creation on the same slice stalls on a synchronous vkCreateBufferView round
trip.

Park destroyed VkBufferViews of buffers created by this encoder in
caboose_view_cache keyed by (device, buffer, flags, format, offset, range,
usage), reusing them on matching vkCreateBufferView requests and destroying
parked views only when their parent VkBuffer or VkDevice is destroyed.
